    {
      "body": "@hnyls2002 @Fridge003 checking in on this breakable-cudagraph bugfix for GLM-5.3-Flash. Its mergeable and just needs run-ci so the suite runs. Could one of you add it and take a look?",
      "created_at": "2026-09-28T16:12:03Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/41218#issuecomment-5873959490",
      "id": 5873959490,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-28T16:12:03Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "reger-men"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@cctry rebased onto current main (head 2f83261) so it clears the CI min base. I re-ran it on MI355X with GLM-5.3-Flash TP4 on top of main e667ab10. With --cuda-graph-backend-decode breakable, unpatched main still dies at decode-graph capture with \"Unsupported BCG output type: LogitsProcessorOutput\". With this patch the server comes up and decode runs through the graph. GSM8K on 100 questions is 0.88 with breakable vs 0.81 for unpatched main on the full decode graph, so no accuracy loss. Its one file, +30 lines. I can't add run-ci, could you add it and take a look?\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-02T16:29:47Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/41218#issuecomment-5956723836",
      "id": 5956723836,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T16:29:47Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "reger-men"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@Oasis-Git @ispobock this fixes --cuda-graph-backend-decode breakable aborting at decode capture with \"Unsupported BCG output type: LogitsProcessorOutput\", I hit it with GLM-5.3-Flash on MI355X. The diff is only breakable_cuda_graph_backend.py and it still has no conflicts after #42286. Could one of you add run-ci and take a look?\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12T15:39:53Z",
